Subject: [PATCH] fix: close worker-session token replay on shared transports +
 enforce TLS on broker/Vault URLs in prod

Second round of Copilot review findings on PR #173:

- security (high): the first review round fixed worker-session token
  replay against the Admin API (requireAuth), but isTransportAuthorized
  -- the shared gate for the SSE, WebSocket, and gRPC transports, all
  of which route an authorized request straight into
  runtimeManager.handleRequest() with full capability access -- had
  the identical gap: signature-only verification, no scope check.
  Mirrors the admin-api.ts fix: explicitly rejects scope:
  'worker-session' tokens. This function had zero prior test coverage;
  added tests/transport-auth.test.ts.

- security (high): UPCLOUD_BROKER_URL and VAULT_ADDR were validated
  with plain z.string().url(), which accepts http://. In production,
  UPCLOUD_BROKER_URL carries the broker's X-API-Key header and all
  session traffic; VAULT_ADDR carries the AppRole client_token and
  every leased secret value. validateConfig()'s existing production
  guard (same block that already requires these vars be set) now also
  requires https://. Dev/test is unaffected -- this only runs inside
  the existing NODE_ENV === 'production' branch. New tests in
  tests/config.test.ts.

- docs (low): CHANGELOG.md undercounted tests/upcloud-worker-factory
  .test.ts's cases (10, should have been 13 after the prior round's
  3 additions). Corrected.

While verifying: tests/config.test.ts's pre-existing "rejects invalid
MCP_TRANSPORT value" test fails identically on the unmodified base
commit (confirmed via git stash) -- unrelated pre-existing bug, not
touched here.

